WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.216
Multi-image layout can now read print dimensions and
quantities directly from filenames.

2
00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:10.927
Chinese, English, and mixed filenames can be
used in the same batch.

3
00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:16.478
This batch uses three original designs.

4
00:00:16.478 --> 00:00:23.141
Artwork numbers remain identifiers, rather than being
mistaken for a print size or quantity.

5
00:00:24.453 --> 00:00:28.555
Open the recognition settings and results
to review each item.

6
00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:35.237
W eight centimeters and P two mean an eight-centimeter width
and two copies, with the original aspect

7
00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:36.296
ratio preserved.

8
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.794
The English filename specifies a
six-centimeter width and three copies.

9
00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:48.051
The Chinese filename specifies seven
centimeters and one copy.

10
00:00:48.051 --> 00:00:52.857
The single-dimension direction and default
unit are also configurable.

11
00:00:53.187 --> 00:00:57.757
Once the values are checked, start the
layout and export a TIFF.

12
00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:04.469
This batch contains six copies across three designs, each
using its own recognized print size.

13
00:01:05.387 --> 00:01:10.236
After generation, the color preview shows
the actual layout output.

14
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:16.534
Print dimensions refer to the artwork itself,
excluding added frames and blank margins.

15
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.630
Switch to the white-ink preview to inspect
the actual W1 channel.

16
00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.273
Both the color artwork and white ink can be
checked before production.
